## Abstract

We investigate the intrinsic magnon spin current in a noncollinear
antiferromagnetic insulator. We introduce a definition of the magnon spin
current in a noncollinear antiferromagnet and find that it is in general
non-conserved, but for certain symmetries and spin polarizations the averaged
effect of non-conserving terms can vanish. We apply this theory to single-layer
potassium iron jarosite \(\mathrm{KFe_3(OH)_6(SO_4)_2}\) and predict a
measurable spin current response.

## Model Hamiltonian

\[
H = \sum_{\langle ij\rangle} J_1\, \mathbf{S}_i\cdot\mathbf{S}_j
  + \sum_{\langle ij\rangle} \mathbf{D}_{ij}\cdot(\mathbf{S}_i\times\mathbf{S}_j)
  + \sum_{\langle\langle ij\rangle\rangle} J_2\, \mathbf{S}_i\cdot\mathbf{S}_j
\]

\[
\mathbf{D}_{ij} = D_p\,\hat{\mathbf{n}}_{ij} + D_z\,\hat{\mathbf{z}}
\]

Canting angle induced by the in-plane DMI:

\[
\eta = \tfrac{1}{2}\tan^{-1}\!\left(\frac{-2D_p}{\sqrt{3}(J_1+J_2)-D_z}\right)\approx 1.9^\circ
\]

Classical noncollinear \(q=0\) order:

\[
\langle\mathbf{S}_i\rangle = S(\cos\eta\cos\phi_i,\ \cos\eta\sin\phi_i,\ \sin\eta),\quad
\phi_A=\tfrac{\pi}{2},\ \phi_B=\tfrac{7\pi}{6},\ \phi_C=-\tfrac{\pi}{6}
\]

## Bosonic BdG structure

Holstein–Primakoff \(\to\) bosonic field
\(\Psi=(b_A,b_B,b_C,b_A^\dagger,b_B^\dagger,b_C^\dagger)^T\). Because of
Bose statistics one diagonalizes \(\sigma_3 H_k\) by a paraunitary \(T_k\):

\[
T_k^\dagger H_k T_k = E_k,\qquad T_k^\dagger \sigma_3 T_k = \sigma_3
\]

## Main result — intrinsic spin Nernst response (Eq. 15)

\[
\Theta_\alpha = \frac{2k_B}{V}\sum_{n=1}^{N}\sum_{k}
  \left(\Omega^{\theta_\alpha}_{n,k}\right)_\beta\,
  c_1\!\left[g(\varepsilon_{n,k})\right]\nabla_\beta T
\]

\[
c_1(x) = (1+x)\ln(1+x) - x\ln(x)
\]

Generalized Berry curvature (Eq. 9):

\[
\left(\Omega^{\theta}_{n,k}\right)^{\alpha}_{\beta}
= \sum_{m\neq n}(\sigma_3)_{nn}(\sigma_3)_{mm}
  \frac{2\,\mathrm{Im}\big[(\theta_\alpha)_{nm}(v_\beta)_{mn}\big]}
       {(\bar\varepsilon_{n,k}-\bar\varepsilon_{m,k})^2}
\]

Spin-current operator:

\[
\hat{j}^{\gamma}_{\lambda} = \tfrac{1}{4}\left(\hat v_\lambda \sigma_3 \hat S^\gamma
  + \hat S^\gamma \sigma_3 \hat v_\lambda\right),\qquad
\hat S^\alpha = -\sigma_0\otimes\mathrm{Diag}(\langle S^\alpha_A\rangle,\langle S^\alpha_B\rangle,\langle S^\alpha_C\rangle)/S
\]

## Numerical results (KFe3(OH)6(SO4)2)

- Parameters \(J_1=3.18\,\mathrm{meV},\ J_2=0.11\,\mathrm{meV},\ |D_p|/J_1=0.062,\ D_z/J_1=-0.062\).
- Chern numbers of the three magnon bands: \(-3,\ 1,\ 2\) (bottom \(\to\) top).
- \(\alpha^{y}_{yx}/k_B\) peaks around \(\sim 3.5\) at \(k_B T/(J_1 S)\sim 1\).
- \(\alpha^{z}_{yx}\) is \(\sim\)two orders of magnitude smaller (small canting).
